# Supporting Responsible AI Use in the Classroom

As students begin learning about and using AI, teachers play an important role in helping students navigate these experiences thoughtfully and responsibly.

These conversations do not require teachers to be AI experts. Instead, the goal is to create a classroom environment where students learn to question information, consider multiple perspectives, reflect on their decisions, and use AI tools responsibly and safely.

The following strategies can help support thoughtful classroom discussions, build digital literacy, and encourage responsible AI use across a variety of topics and learning experiences.

<div style="display:grid; gap:16px; max-width:90%; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; color:#292F36;">

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:start; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/84520ba319601b9428dadd482d217453-Screenshot 2026-05-21 at 9.42.16 AM.png" style="width:175px; height:175px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Encourage Multiple Perspectives</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
Help students consider who benefits, who may be affected differently, and how the same technology can lead to different outcomes for different people.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Identifying groups impacted by an AI system</li>
<li>Considering benefits alongside risks</li>
<li>Exploring how personal experiences shape perspectives</li>
<li>Discussing trade-offs instead of looking for one “right” answer</li>
<li>Reflecting on fairness, representation, and access</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:start; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/3ce695c37af91b664ed10c78fe1e733f-Screenshot 2026-05-21 at 9.42.40 AM.png" style="width:175px; height:175px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Encourage Verification and Critical Thinking</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
Support students in questioning and evaluating AI-generated information rather than accepting it at face value.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Asking, “How do we know this is accurate?”</li>
<li>Comparing information across multiple sources</li>
<li>Looking for missing context, bias, or misleading details</li>
<li>Discussing why AI tools sometimes generate inaccurate or incomplete responses</li>
<li>Reinforcing that AI is a tool, not a final source of truth</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:start; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/33608b33f32a20644acd84f8802c73ee-Screenshot 2026-05-21 at 9.42.45 AM.png" style="width:175px; height:175px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Use “What-If” Scenarios</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
Use hypothetical situations to explore how AI decisions and design choices can shape outcomes.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Testing how different prompts or inputs change results</li>
<li>Exploring impacts on different groups or situations</li>
<li>Comparing possible benefits and harms</li>
<li>Discussing how AI-generated media could be misunderstood or misused</li>
<li>Considering how privacy or safety concerns might arise in different scenarios</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:start; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/d4542349e9d7e9073843b4d971d76ea3-Screenshot 2026-05-21 at 9.42.49 AM.png" style="width:175px; height:175px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Promote Responsible and Safe Use</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
Help students understand that how they use AI tools matters.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Discussing what information should remain private</li>
<li>Setting expectations for appropriate AI use in the classroom</li>
<li>Modeling safe and thoughtful technology use</li>
<li>Reinforcing accountability and responsible decision-making</li>
<li>Encouraging students to ask questions when unsure what is appropriate to share or create</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:start; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/8500a2f4d9da1259b470b62df1c1d791-Screenshot 2026-05-21 at 9.42.54 AM.png" style="width:175px; height:175px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Acknowledge Uncertainty and Complexity</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
Emphasize that many AI-related questions do not have simple or clear answers.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">This might include:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>Normalizing uncertainty and ongoing learning</li>
<li>Encouraging questioning and reflection</li>
<li>Supporting respectful discussion when opinions differ</li>
<li>Helping students navigate ambiguity thoughtfully</li>
<li>Focusing on inquiry and exploration rather than certainty</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:220px 1fr; gap:16px; border:2px solid #8C52BA; border-radius:16px; padding:18px; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">
<div style="display:flex; align-items:start; justify-content:center; padding:10px;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/e7c1e0f04192b4ec2206d37102fa42b3-Screenshot 2026-05-21 at 9.42.58 AM.png" style="width:175px; height:175px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:22px; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:8px; color:#141414;">Create Space for Reflection and Discussion</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:10px;">
Encourage students to reflect on how AI influences their thinking, decisions, and interactions with information.
</div>
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px;">You might ask:</div>
<ul style="margin:0 0 12px 20px; padding:0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
<li>How did AI influence your thinking?</li>
<li>What information or sources do you trust most, and why?</li>
<li>What responsibilities come with using AI tools?</li>
<li>How is interacting with AI different from interacting with a person?</li>
<li>When should we question or verify what AI produces?</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

</div>

<br>

> **💬 Quick Reflection:** Which of these stratagies fits easiest into your teaching style?
>
> By guiding these discussions with openness and curiosity, you will help students develop a thoughtful, ethical approach to AI technology.
MARKDOWN
